.TH IMPROV-ADD-MEASURE 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-add\-measure \- Add an input measure
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov add\-measure\fR <db> <id> <name> <type> <input> [category]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add an input measure.
.PP
Its type says how set parses its values. The word input is required, after the type and before the categories it ranges over, which follow by name: add\-measure m.db 101 Quantity number input Time Product.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIdb\fR>
The model store: a file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
<\fIid\fR>
The measure\*(Aqs numeric id
.TP
<\fIname\fR>
The measure\*(Aqs name
.TP
<\fItype\fR>
number, boolean or text
.TP
<\fIinput\fR>
The word input
.TP
[\fIcategory\fR]
The categories the measure ranges over, by name
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1).
